# Angular ESLint Best Practices

## Source Attribution
**Source**: [Context7 - Angular ESLint](https://context7.com/angular-eslint/angular-eslint)
**Purpose**: Comprehensive ESLint configuration and usage guidelines for Angular projects

## ESLint Configuration Fundamentals

### 1. ESLint Setup
```json
// ✅ ESLint configuration example
{
  "root": true,
  "ignorePatterns": ["projects/**/*"],
  "overrides": [
    {
      "files": ["*.ts"],
      "parserOptions": {
        "project": ["tsconfig.json"],
        "createDefaultProgram": true
      },
      "extends": [
        "plugin:@angular-eslint/recommended",
        "plugin:@angular-eslint/template/process-inline-templates"
      ],
      "rules": {
        "@angular-eslint/component-class-suffix": ["error", { "suffixes": ["Component"] }],
        "@angular-eslint/directive-class-suffix": ["error", { "suffixes": ["Directive"] }],
        "@angular-eslint/no-empty-lifecycle-method": "warn",
        "@typescript-eslint/explicit-function-return-type": "error",
        "@typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars": "warn",
        "@typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any": "error",
        "@typescript-eslint/consistent-type-definitions": ["error", "interface"]
      }
    },
    {
      "files": ["*.html"],
      "extends": ["plugin:@angular-eslint/template/recommended"],
      "rules": {
        "@angular-eslint/template/accessible-name": "error",
        "@angular-eslint/template/alt-text": "error",
        "@angular-eslint/template/no-positive-tabindex": "error"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

### 2. Linting Best Practices
- Use the official `@angular-eslint` plugin for Angular projects
- Enforce component and directive suffixes
- Disallow empty lifecycle methods
- Require explicit function return types
- Disallow usage of `any` type
- Prefer interfaces over type aliases
- Disallow unused variables
- Enforce accessibility rules in templates
- Use Prettier for consistent formatting
- Integrate linting into CI/CD pipelines
- Run linting before every commit

### 3. Common Rules
- `@angular-eslint/component-class-suffix`: Enforce `Component` suffix for components
- `@angular-eslint/directive-class-suffix`: Enforce `Directive` suffix for directives
- `@angular-eslint/no-empty-lifecycle-method`: Warn on empty lifecycle methods
- `@typescript-eslint/explicit-function-return-type`: Require explicit return types
- `@typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars`: Warn on unused variables
- `@typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any`: Disallow `any` type
- `@typescript-eslint/consistent-type-definitions`: Prefer `interface` over `type`
- `@angular-eslint/template/accessible-name`: Enforce accessible names in templates
- `@angular-eslint/template/alt-text`: Require alt text for images
- `@angular-eslint/template/no-positive-tabindex`: Disallow positive tabindex

### 4. Linting in Practice
```bash
# ✅ Run linting
ng lint

# ✅ Fix lint errors automatically
ng lint --fix

# ✅ Run linting on staged files (with lint-staged)
npx lint-staged
```

### 5. Linting and Formatting Integration
- Use Prettier with ESLint for consistent code formatting
- Add Prettier config (`.prettierrc`) and ignore file (`.prettierignore`)
- Integrate with VSCode extensions for auto-formatting
- Add lint and format scripts to `package.json`

### 6. Testing Lint Rules
```typescript
// ✅ Testing lint rules with custom test cases
describe('ESLint Rules', () => {
  it('should enforce component class suffix', () => {
    // ...test implementation
  });
});
```

## Best Practices Summary

### Do's ✅
- Use official Angular ESLint plugin
- Enforce naming conventions
- Require explicit return types
- Disallow `any` type
- Prefer interfaces
- Enforce accessibility in templates
- Integrate linting into CI/CD
- Use Prettier for formatting
- Test custom lint rules

### Don'ts ❌
- Ignore lint errors
- Use `any` type
- Skip accessibility rules
- Use inconsistent formatting
- Skip linting in CI/CD
- Use type aliases for objects
- Allow empty lifecycle methods
- Use positive tabindex

This comprehensive guide ensures proper ESLint usage and configuration for Angular projects following best practices.
